      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes complete sense that your poem feels disconnected; your words are likely trying to process a depth of exhaustion that poetry often struggles to capture directly. That feeling of being trapped in an endless loop is the very raw material many artists use to find that profound beauty you're describing, but recognizing it might feel like a trap until it fully transforms. Your work doesn't need to force itself into a shape of certainty right now; instead, allow the exhaustion itself to serve as the truth that anchors the piece.",
